       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg PO total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a more typical regimen\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
